proves.  \n• Allocate a portion to Consumer Discretionary exposures to benefit from enhanced consumer spending post-recovery.  \n• Consider defensive positioning with longer-duration Treasuries or bond ETFs (e.g., IEF) to hedge against potential rate hikes or renewed uncertainty.  \n• Use options strategies (e.g., protective puts or calls) to manage downside risk in equity positions amid mixed Fed signals.  \n• Stay nimble: Regularly reassess the Fed’s communication and geopolitical developments, and be ready to rebalance positions should the risk landscape shift.\n\nOverall, a balanced approach—with a tilt towards quality growth sectors and tactical risk management—appears best suited for navigating current market conditions."
